        ],
        "source_refs": [],
        "body": "The six settlements and four factions remain a regional proposal, not the whole planet. Their useful differences survive the milestone, but their relationship to a local owner becomes more specific.\n\n**Tinwater / Foundry / Two Nets:** complete first projects, ordinary stock, included receiving and useful bench sessions. The local return route should not demand exact lineage documentation before a novice can clean and refit known anatomy.\n\n**Cinderhouse / Rivet Commons:** support and force under load, repeat dimensions, root adaptation and paid workshop work. More substantial reinforcement is useful only when it transmits actual loads without binding. The civic faction does not own all private stock.\n\n**Crown Basin / Reedwater Compact:** full stage-aware supply and flight preparation. A returning Flyer can obtain specialist root matching or supported emergence without creating a private pond. Ground racers still live and race there.\n\n**Saltglass / Lantern Exchange:** distinct product promises, rematching, appearance-led work and historical descriptions. A beautifully presented ordinary animal remains an honest offering; accurate descriptions make travel and consignment useful.\n\n**Spanrest / Traverse Freeholds:** portable support, receiving, joint work and keep-running arrangements. A traveler can book actual work instead of acquiring a new profession. A portable section collection is owned construction, not permission to invent unlimited venues.\n\n**New World City:** championship grids coexist with neighborhood competition, markets, benches and displays. A maker can visit without a world berth. A representative receives promised support without receiving every premium part. Returning home does not delete the racer’s public identity.\n\n## Source availability is an authored economy, not an inventory reset\n\nA patch supplies a population with actual cohorts. A Wrangloid supplies actual stock from specified sources or an explicitly modeled ordinary production boundary. A retailer may carry known prepared anatomy even when the player has never visited its habitat. Unmeasured wild stock and a seller’s measured stock can have different evidence, not different laws of inheritance.\n\nWhere a producer aggregates ordinary output, the world still needs its life-stage inputs and feasible supply. Aggregation can reduce simulation cost; it cannot grant a worker-only bee box a self-reproducing colony or allow the same host pupa to become both a Bankseed adult and a consumed Caustic developmental input.\n\n## A public vocabulary, not a licensing monopoly\n\nShared pattern names, fitting ranges and product cards let people work across factions. They do not own assimilation. A novel Open construction may remain outside commercial patterns if it has real anatomy and meets the event’s actual conditions.\n\nMixed-source repairs and imported stock are normal possibilities. Their provenance remains detailed enough for the relevant question without requiring a complete scientific paper before ordinary trade. Precision is purchased where it changes a promise, not charged as a toll on every interaction."
      },
