        "source_refs": [],
        "body": "The old cumulative decision records remain intact. Their original `unresolved` labels cannot be read as proof that the subsequent source, material and sporting volumes contain no answers. Equally, a detailed proposal is not automatically author-approved canon.\n\nThe new [Decision Resolution Register](RRR_Wave_20_Resolution_Register.md) separates each broad decision into developed subquestions and genuinely open choices.\n\n| Decision | Current usable reference | Still open |\n|---|---|---|\n| D01: biosphere | Current populations require actual food, water and development inputs. H30 means thirty years after the founding sport story. | Which proposed recovery history is adopted; wider chronology. |\n| D02: scale | Bench-built and hand-carried is the working relation. | Absolute dimensions; W19’s preferred study range remains unadopted. |\n| D03: assimilation | Innate incorporation, prepared roots, support/supply/control and ordinary exchange are defined. | Absolute rates and the full physiological mechanism. |\n| D04: removal/storage | Whole donor, detached component, exchange support, material classes and part-specific service are differentiated. | Product viability curves, full raw-removal consequences and universal renewal policy. |\n| D05: heredity | Species-specific units, acquired-graft separation, observed parentage and complementary selection are defined. | Numerical architecture and prevalence for each form. |\n| D06: life stages | Twenty source monographs and the Bankseed support note exist. | Full ecology, unlisted sources and calibrated distributions. |\n| D07: life course | Ordinary service, local function loss, repair, original material, known terminal preparation and return decisions are defined. | Host aging, irreversible mortality, severe risk policy and rare-material regrowth. |\n| D08: control | Native competence and required actual sensing/actuation are defined. | Final player intervention and detailed learned behavior. |\n| D09: time | Default offline pause; one in-world continuity for actual activity and support. | Session times, biological pacing, and an optional offline mode. |\n| D10: trade/information | Actual ownership, carriers, receiving, source evidence, funded purposes and return routes are defined. | Full route durations, large-world budgets and communication reach. |\n| D11: representation | W19’s entrant/host/build/seat charter is the current regional proposal. | Wider signatories and final adoption of quotas. |\n| D12: event boundaries | Independent locomotion/equipment/progression/format; finish-first; no universal Open part cap. | Final capability thresholds, dimensions and severe-event policies. |\n\n## Three life-course directions, not three hidden defaults\n\n**L0 — Recoverable ordinary campaign, severe policy reserved.** Recommended direction for the next experience study: routine supported rebuilding and ordinary setbacks are recoverable; meaningful component loss can occur under declared mechanisms; severe host outcomes remain explicitly unresolved until authored. This is not invulnerability and cannot authorize a concealed fatality roll.\n\n**L1 — Universal biological aging and severe loss.** Potentially coherent, but it must supply life histories, care, replacement paths, event disclosure, remembrance and progression that do not reduce every beloved build to a forced expiry timer. Real insect lifespans are not game clocks. Not adopted.\n\n**L2 — Regeneration-forward host biology.** Could emphasize the mutation, but it needs actual resource, time, identity and pattern-retention rules. It must say whether a rare structure is repaired, copied or replaced and why original acquisition remains valuable. Not adopted.\n\nThe material and return definitions in this milestone are useful under several eventual choices. They do not finish the choice by omission. Before play calibration, the selected policy must be stated explicitly to the user and development team."
