        "id": "W20.CH.HANDOFF",
        "title": "14. How the next team uses this edition",
        "status": "current_working_compendium_definition",
        "prior_refs": [
          "W15.SYSTEM.RETURN",
          "W19.SCOPE.CULTURE"
        ],
        "source_refs": [],
        "body": "This milestone is a rewritten current desk reference, not another pile of unranked rules. It has three entry routes.\n\n**Build a racer:** use the translation contract, component passport and product brief. Follow its actual source only when designing acquisition or production.\n\n**Design a consequence:** use the local cause, required function, offered return route, actual material input and opportunity case. Do not infer an entire death model from one fracture.\n\n**Extend the world:** choose a new source, institution or course because it supplies a different meaningful possibility. Reuse the shared anatomy and participation rules; state the new facts and what they replace.\n\n## Minimum handoff packet for one new feature\n\n1. The particular user desire and a complete achievable outcome.\n2. The source-hobby function or explicitly RRR-native extension.\n3. The actual objects and their identity across the activity.\n4. The anatomical mechanism, inputs and working situation.\n5. What the player can observe, what remains unknown and how additional information helps.\n6. At least one affordable or service-based participation route and one optional expert route.\n7. A meaningful failure, a valid fallback and the material/cash consequences.\n8. An enabling case, a non-enabling case, and an altered-build comparison that the later implementation must demonstrate.\n\nThese are authoring fields, not eight UI prompts. Shared records make the game simpler to present because the content agrees before a screen is built.\n\n## Editorial acceptance\n\nThe companion ledger identifies twenty substantive current-reference amendments and their earlier scopes. Thirty-four use-and-service entries cover the thirty foundational preparations and four explicit flight preparation supplements. Each includes source, mechanism, changed-condition example, response and remaining value. Eight product briefs list actual included/native roles. Six cross-volume reference cases follow the same objects through ordinary and adverse outcomes. The current interpretation JSON points to the appropriate local records rather than asking an agent to merge all historical rules indiscriminately.\n\nProgrammatic checks can confirm identifiers, links, prior-file preservation and arithmetic. They cannot establish fun, fairness, retention, real physiology or sustainable pricing. No runtime suite is rerun here and no old test count is presented as evidence that this new experience works.\n\n## Next authored block\n\nDefine a bounded set of ordinary event-and-service days spanning Tinwater, Cinderhouse, Saltglass and Crown Basin, including a first kit, a returning racer, a breeder with actual surplus and a customer receiving a product. Use this edition’s condition and identity rules. Add qualitative sequence and actual resource offers before choosing timing or numerical risk.\n\nThen carry the selected severe-outcome/scale decisions into the corresponding dimensioned and experience studies when the author chooses those directions. Do not disguise another prototype as completion of the world bible."
      }
